  "details": "Hello, I have my own mini-server on linux on which nginx is installed. The process of how I transport video to the global Internet - I turn on nginx, run serveo.net (https://serveo.net / . Connect the local servers to the Internet), I find the video in the url directory and can watch it in the browser. I used serveo.net due to the fact that only legal entities can have a static ip address in my region. And my friend who has a server with a static ip can run videos in Vrchat without third-party services(serveo.net ). If possible, please ask the Vrchat developers to add to the whitelists - serveo.net .In order for those who are unable to have a static/white ip address for various reasons, they were given the opportunity to enjoy watching movies, TV series, and anime with their family and friends.",
